{{!-- Sign in, in the four states the design draws.

THE STATES ARE GHOST'S CLASSES, NOT A SCRIPT'S. The reference build drives them from an Alpine
value because it has no server to talk to; here Portal owns the submit and reports back by putting
`loading`, then exactly one of `success` or `error`, on the form element — read out of portal 2.71
rather than from documentation, and recorded beside the three rules the footer's form needed. So
every state is real markup that CSS reveals, and `assets/css/screen.css` holds the whole of the
theme's side.

That is also why the success panel is a SIBLING of the form rather than a child: on success the
form is hidden and the panel takes its place, which is an adjacent-sibling selector and nothing
more.

`data-members-email` is not optional. Without it Portal finds no address on submit and the form
silently no-ops while looking complete.

The address in "we sent a link to …" is written by the theme's own script, because Portal reports
the outcome and not the input. One line of enhancement over markup that already reads correctly
without it. --}}
<form
	data-members-form="signin"
	class="flex flex-col gap-[18px]">
	<div
		role="alert"
		aria-live="assertive"
		class="members-error-panel border-danger-border border-l-danger bg-danger-soft rounded-sm border border-l-[3px] px-[18px] py-4">
		<p class="font-ui text-danger text-sm font-semibold">{{t "We could not send that link"}}</p>
		<p
			class="font-ui text-muted mt-2 text-[13.5px] leading-[1.55]"
			data-members-error></p>
	</div>

	<div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
		<label
			for="signin-email"
			class="font-ui text-[13.5px] font-semibold">{{t "Email address"}}</label>
		<input
			id="signin-email"
			name="email"
			type="email"
			data-members-email
			autocomplete="email"
			required
			aria-describedby="signin-help"
			placeholder="{{t "you@publication.com"}}"
			class="font-ui bg-bg text-text border-border w-full rounded-sm border px-[15px] py-[13px] text-[15.5px]">
		<p
			id="signin-help"
			class="font-ui text-muted text-[12.5px]">{{t "We'll email you a link that signs you in. No password to remember."}}</p>
	</div>

	<button
		type="submit"
		class="btn btn-primary font-ui flex cursor-pointer items-center justify-center gap-2.5 rounded-sm border px-[22px] py-3.5 text-[15px] font-semibold">
		<span
			aria-hidden="true"
			class="members-spinner spinner size-3.5 rounded-full border-2 border-current"></span>
		<span class="members-idle">{{t "Email me a sign-in link"}}</span>
		<span class="members-busy">{{t "Sending link…"}}</span>
	</button>

	<p
		aria-live="polite"
		class="font-ui text-muted members-busy min-h-[1em] text-center text-[12.5px]">{{t "Sending your sign-in link…"}}</p>
</form>

<div
	role="status"
	aria-live="polite"
	class="members-success text-center">
	<p class="text-accent font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.1em] uppercase">{{t "Link sent"}}</p>

	<h2 class="font-display tracking-heading mt-3.5 text-2xl leading-[1.2] font-medium">{{t "Check your email"}}</h2>

	<p class="text-small text-muted mx-auto mt-3.5 max-w-[38ch] leading-[1.65] text-pretty">
		{{~t "We sent a sign-in link to"}}
		<strong
			class="text-text"
			data-members-sent-to>{{t "the address you entered"}}</strong>. {{t "It expires in 24 hours and works once."~}}
	</p>
</div>
